    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as our undisputed anchor. Boasting a stellar 84.24 score, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a high-leverage spot in the three-hole against Baz, positioning him to capitalize on early scoring opportunities. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy, where **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.85) and **Caleb Durbin** (70.40) represent elite efficiency plays. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against a right-handed arm, while **Caleb Durbin** is poised to exploit an 8.21 xERA from Wilkinson, making him an ideal candidate to drive our SB category in what should be a high-scoring affair.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing efficiency over raw volume to preserve game caps. **Carson Benge** (41.92) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly failing to displace our lower-ceiling utility plays; however, his poor platoon split (L/L) against Newcomb ultimately pushed him below the optimal threshold. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (56.07) remains in the lineup despite a sub-optimal platoon matchup against Basso; his elite 0.459 xwOBA provides a floor that overrides the L/L penalty. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** closely, as both rely on projected lineup spots\u2014if **Gary Sanchez** slides down the order or **Christian Yelich** receives a surprise rest day, we are prepared to pivot to more favorable bench options. We continue to hold **Josh Smith** on the IL, awaiting further updates, while **Colt Keith** remains sidelined and excluded from today's active rotation.",
